WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.180
Companies will have to take in terms of how they launch or ultimately progress, you know,

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.180
medicines.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:10.160
We're already in a situation where, depending on how you look, 30 to 40 percent of medicines

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.640
in Europe available in the U.S. don't ultimately come to Europe.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.780
You could have that number grow.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:21.980
In general, significant delays for introduction of medicines into the European Union.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.920
So there's a lot of work to do.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:28.620
We certainly have, I think, proposals to all the key governments and most important in

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:29.980
my mind are Japan and Germany.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.920
But we haven't seen the progress that we need to see.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:37.160
So this is something we'll have to continue to advocate for over the next year because

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.360
I think it's really a 2027 story where you start to see the impact of MFN on launches

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.360
in Europe.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.380
Next question.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:49.380
Thank you.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:54.380
Your next question comes from the line of James Gordon from Barclays.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.380
Please go ahead.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.200
Hello.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.200
I'm James Gordon from Barclays.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.200
Thanks for taking the question.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.000
The question was on hormonal breast cancer.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.000
So, you know, I think it's really important.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.080
The question is, how do you know that you can get the right amount of the right amount

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.080
of MFN for breast cancer?

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.080
So what should we expect to have?

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:07.080
Chirogesterone as U.S. approval for adjuvant hormonal breast cancer.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.080
Well before the U.N. because they've used a PRV.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.080
And it's suggesting this could be an $11 billion plus product across the adjuvant and second

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:12.560
line, but mostly in adjuvant.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:15.600
So then that seems to assume big board uptake.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:21.040
I think the logic is that that could be used instead of someone using an aromatase and

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.960
a CDK4 for some of the patients.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.080
So based on what you know about hormonal breast cancer, do you think that's plausible?

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.980
Do you think is it even from the end of this year you could see some pressure on CDK4?

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.460
K4 use because people instead would just do a CERN. So any thoughts on that, please?

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:44.690
Yeah, we don't see that in the same way. I mean, what we expect, continue to expect,

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:51.710
is that physicians will want to use something to ultimately impact the hormonal access and

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:56.250
then subsequently the cell cyclin-dependent kinase access, especially for patients that

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:02.010
we're talking about here, which are patients that are node zero, node one, node two, or more,

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:07.370
and have other risk factors that indicate they have a higher risk of recurrence of breast cancer.

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:12.810
So that's point one. That's all of our market research suggests that. And I think part of

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:19.050
the reason the major oral CERN companies are partnering with us to do combination studies

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:25.290
is they ultimately see it in a similar way as well. I can't comment on patients who are very

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:31.270
early or less high-risk early breast cancer patients. We used to call them kind of stage one.

